Annotation(rdfs:comment "Testing approach where occupancy and composition and levels phenotypes are all grouped as siblings under a abnormal glycosylation parent.  This approach should simplify integration with HPO.

The challenge remains w.r.t. confusion around when to annotate to a level vs a composition phenotype (e.g. abnormal fucosylated glycan levels vs abnormal glycan fucose content), but we can try to clarify the rules here, and see what feedback we get when  we test.  Also, it may be fine just to say annotate to both if both would apply, and this doesn't really hurt anything.")

