# Class: obo:CHEBItemp_0002236 (glycan antenna)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBItemp_0002236 "The branch or antenna component of a glycan chain, which extends the glycan 'core'.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002037 obo:CHEBItemp_0002236 "antennary glycan group")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBItemp_0002236 "glycan antenna"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBItemp_0002236 obo:CHEBItemp_0002164)

# Class: obo:CHEBItemp_0002237 (glycan core)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBItemp_0002237 "The 'core' of an N- or O- glycan chain, containing residues between the aglycone attachment point and extended/branched antennary regions of the glycan.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002037 obo:CHEBItemp_0002237 "core glycan group")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBItemp_0002237 "glycan core"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBItemp_0002237 obo:CHEBItemp_0002164)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0001001 (Phenotype)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0001001 "Phenotype"@en)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002001 (abnormal glycan metabolism)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002001 "An abnormality in the process of glycan catabolism or biosynthesis.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002001 "abnormal glycan metabolism"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002001 obo:MGPO_0002028)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002002 (abnormal glycan level)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002002 "An increase or decrease in the amount of a type or specific species of glycan present in the body, cell, or specific compartment  therein.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002032 obo:MGPO_0002002 "Here we make distinction between free and conjugated only deeper in the hierarchy - since often we don’t know origin. Often MS-based phenotypes simply refer to altered levels of a class of glycans - and these clearly go here. Other cases are trickier - e.g. elevated levels of mannose rich cores species. Here, if an MS-based phenotype cannot be best characterized with a residue-specific composition class, they should be documented here as a levels phenotype. Challenge is that the curator has to understand the expert interpretation of thee data to make selection here, and these interpretations can be quite nuanced/subjective.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002002 "abnormal glycan levels"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002002 obo:MGPO_0001001)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002003 (abnormal glycan occupancy)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002003 "An increase or decrease in the number of glycan chains conjugated to an aglycone target.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002032 obo:MGPO_0002003 "Relevant Classification Axes (in order shown for exemplar classes below):
1  glycosylation/target type (N-linked vs O-linked vs proteoglycan)
1.1  glycosylated residue (e.g. Asn, Ser, Thr)
1.2  specific aglycone target (e.g. transferrin)
1.2.1  anatomical/cellular location (e.g. serum, golgi)
")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:MGPO_0002003 "\"Occupancy\" is used here to describe the extent of conjugation of a glycan chain to glycosylation sites on an aglycone target. Abnormal occupancy does not speak to the structure or composition of the glycan chain, just the relative abundance of glycan chains on some protein or lipid target.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002003 "abnormal glycan occupancy"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002003 obo:MGPO_0002009)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002004 (abnormal glycan structure)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:MGPO_0002004 "A change in the molecular structure of a glycan, including altered sugar composition, chain length, linkage or branching patterns, or modifications on a sugar residues")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:MGPO_0002004 "Former logical definition:

'has part' some 
    (structure
     and ('has modifier' some abnormal)
     and ('inheres in' some glycan))")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:MGPO_0002004 "The distinction between abnormal glycan levels and abnormal glycan structure/composition is confounded by the fact that specific phenotypes in both categories are typically reported in the literature by describing  the amount of a particular type of glycan. For example, \"increased sialylated oligosaccharides in the lysosome\" is verbatim text reporting a ‘compositional’ defect, and \"increased levels of complex N-Glycans in the serum\"  is verbatim text reporting a ‘level’ defect. The key difference is that the former defect indicates that glycans contain abnormalities in their sialyl content that make them compositionally different that glycan end products normally found in the lysosome. And biologically, this defect likely results from defects in glycosylation, deglycosylation, or isomerase enzymes.  By contrast, the latter defect does not reflect a structural/compositional abnormality in the specified glycan, but rather that the level of a certain normal type of glycan end-product is elevated. Compared to a compositional phenotype, this defect likely has a very different biological cause related to abnormal glycan degradation or trafficking.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002004 "abnormal glycan structure"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002004 obo:MGPO_0002028)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002005 (abnormal glycan-related process)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002005 "Abnormality in a biological process that has a glycan or glycan-containing entity as a product or active  participant.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002005 "abnormal glycan-related process"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002005 obo:MGPO_0002028)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002006 (abnormal glycan binding)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002006 "An abnormality in the process of a glycan binding to its target.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002006 "abnormal glycan binding"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002006 obo:MGPO_0002005)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002007 (abnormal deglycosylation)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002007 "An abnormality in the process of glycan deglycosylation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002007 "abnormal deglycosylation"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002007 obo:MGPO_0002028)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002008 (abnormal glycan catabolism)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002008 "abnormal glycan catabolism"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002008 obo:MGPO_0002001)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002009 (abnormal glycosylation)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002009 "An abnormality in the structure or composition of glycans, or their attachment to aglycone conjugation targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002032 obo:MGPO_0002009 "Can we logically define this . . . a ssome abnormal structure that inheres in some molecular entity that has part some gycan? This wont work if we have the abnormal glycosylation activity phenotypes in this hierarchy.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002037 obo:MGPO_0002009 "abnormal glycan structure")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002037 obo:MGPO_0002009 "abnormal glycosylation structure")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:MGPO_0002009 "Abnormal glycosylation phenotypes cover altered glycan composition, including altered sugar residue content, chain length, linkage, or branching patterns, as well as altered occupancy, characterized by abnormal degree or pattens or conjugation of glycan chains to aglycone targets.

Abnormal glycosylation phenotypes typically result from defects in the machinery that directly (glycosyltransferase, glycosidase, oligosaccharyltransferase enzymes) or indierctly (isomerasaes, transport proteins, chaperones, glycan residue synthesis/activation pathways, etc.) contribute to the building/remodeling of glycan chains, or their attachement to aglycone targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002009 "abnormal glycosylation"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002009 obo:MGPO_0001001)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002010 (abnormal glycan branching)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002010 "A change in the structure of a glycan chain due to altered branching patterns. ")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002032 obo:MGPO_0002010 "Relevant Classification Axes (in order shown for exemplar classes above):
1  attachment (conjugated vs free glycans)
1.1  aglycone class (e.g. glycoprotein-linked vs glycopeptide-linked)
1.1.1  more specific aglycone class (e.g. N-glycan  vs O-glycan for proteins)
")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002010 "abnormal glycan branching"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002010 obo:MGPO_0002009)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002011 (abnormal glycan composition)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002011 "A change in the strucutre of a glycan chain due to variations in number and/or type of sugar residue constituents - typically an increased or decreased abundance of a given type of residue, or the substitution of on residue type for another.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:MGPO_0002037 obo:MGPO_0002011 "abnormal glycan chain composition")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:MGPO_0002011 "abnormal glycosylation of glycans")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002011 "abnormal glycan composition"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002011 obo:MGPO_0002009)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002012 (abnormal N-linked glycoprotein occupancy)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002012 "An increase or decrease in the number of N-glycan chains conjugated to aglycone targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002012 "abnormal N-linked glycoprotein occupancy"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002012 obo:MGPO_0002201)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002013 (abnormal O-linked glycoprotein occupancy)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002013 "An increase or decrease in the number of O-glycan chains conjugated to aglycone targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002013 "abnormal O-linked glycoprotein occupancy"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002013 obo:MGPO_0002202)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002017 (abnormal IDUA activity)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002017 "Altered IDUA enzymatic activity in an organism, cell, or part thereof.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002017 "abnormal IDUA activity"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002017 obo:MGPO_0002036)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002018 (abnormal heparan sulfate degradation)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002018 "abnormal heparan sulfate degradation"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002018 obo:MGPO_0002008)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002019 (abnormal R-type lectin binding)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002019 "abnormal R-type lectin binding"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002019 obo:MGPO_0002006)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002023 (abnormal transferrin N-glycan occupancy)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002023 "An increase or decrease in the number of N-glycan chains conjugated to transferrin protein.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002023 "abnormal transferrin N-glycan occupancy"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002023 obo:MGPO_0002028)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002024 (abnormal serum transferrin N-glycan occupancy)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002024 "An increase or decrease in the number of N-glycan chains conjugated to transferrin protein in blood serum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002024 "abnormal serum transferrin N-glycan occupancy"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002024 obo:MGPO_0002023)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002027 (abnormal golgi biantennary N-glycan levels)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002027 "An increase or decrease in the amount or concentration of normal biantennary N-gycan structures present in the golgi complex.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002027 "abnormal golgi biantennary N-glycan levels"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:MGPO_0002027 obo:MGPO_0002028)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002028 (DeprecatedClass)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:MGPO_0002028 "DeprecatedClass"@en)

# Class: obo:MGPO_0002029 (abnormal glycan-related activity)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MGPO_0002029 "An alteration in the activity of a molecular entity such as an enzyme or transporter protein that acts on glycans or glycan-containing entities.")
